Content-type: text/plain;
	charset="UTF-8"
Content-transfer-encoding: quoted-printable

One question that I have after reading it: I understand why one wants to im=
plement this extension, but I don=E2=80=99t see how the two endpoints would arrive=
 at that external PSK.=20

Sadly - we're back to the 1980's in terms of key management.   The obvious =
answers are a) they meet to exchange keys, b) they're given a key through a =
KDC, c) they get them in the mail. (and I'm really not kidding about (c))

I don=E2=80=99t think I get it. There=E2=80=99s a ton of submissions at NIST PQC, most =
came with some formal proofs. I can=E2=80=99t believe none of them is good enough.=
 Anything from that pool should be better than nothing=E2=80=A6?

Also, if you do have a running KDC, why would you want/need TLS 1.3 ECDHE i=
n addition to it?=20

Would such a pre-shared key be long-term (i.e., good/used for many connecti=
ons), or is it going to be a use-once thing?

=20

=20

From: TLS <tls-bounces@ietf.org> on behalf of Russ Housley <housley@vigilse=
c.com>
Date: Monday, May 20, 2019 at 3:21 PM
To: Joe Salowey <joe@salowey.net>
Cc: IETF TLS <tls@ietf.org>
Subject: Re: [TLS] WGLC for draft-ietf-tls-tls13-cert-with-extern-psk

=20

TLS 1.3 Extension for Certificate-based Authentication with an External PSK=
 ensures the US Government has a quantum-resistant option for TLS in the int=
erim years until post-quantum algorithms emerge from the NIST process. For t=
his reason, there is an intent to specify this extension in future procureme=
nts.

=20

Russ

=20




On May 15, 2019, at 9:20 AM, Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net> wrote:

=20

The last call has come and gone without any comment.  Please indicate if yo=
u have reviewed the draft even if you do not have issues to raise so the cha=
irs can see who has reviewed it.  Also indicate if you have any plans to imp=
lement the draft.=20

=20

On Tue, Apr 9, 2019 at 8:51 PM Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net> wrote:

This is the working group last call for the "TLS 1.3 Extension for Certific=
ate-based Authentication with an External Pre-Shared Key=E2=80=9D draft available =
at https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-cert-with-extern-ps=
k/. Please review the document and send your comments to the list by 2359 UT=
C on 23 April 2019.

=20

Thanks,
Chris, Joe, and Sean







_______________________________________________
TLS mailing list
TLS@ietf.org
https://www.ietf.org/mailman/listinfo/tls
=20


--B_3641217109_1126335286
